DXVK 601930949d111edbbcf9dd463948426d9f8f6ddd

A shared D3D11 resource on a driver without VK_KHR_external_memory_win32
(the PS5's RADV has no external memory) is refused by canShareImage, which
logs "Failed to create shared resource" and leaves m_shared false; the image
is then created as an ordinary one. createImageResource was still told the
requested handle type, so it called initKmtHandles, which calls
vkGetMemoryWin32HandleKHR, a function pointer that is null when the
extension is not enabled: a call through null, a crash at start in Unity
games (a Unity game, 2026-10-12). Ask for a handle only when the image is
shared; the image then falls back to a private one, as the log already says.

--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_image.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_image.cpp
@@ -334,7 +334,9 @@
     allocationInfo.resourceCookie = cookie();
     allocationInfo.properties = m_properties;
     allocationInfo.mode = mode;
-    allocationInfo.handleType = m_info.sharing.type;
+    allocationInfo.handleType = m_shared
+      ? m_info.sharing.type
+      : VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_FLAG_BITS_MAX_ENUM;
 
     if (m_info.transient)
       allocationInfo.mode.set(DxvkAllocationMode::NoDedicated);
